-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC # Preparing TPC-DI

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Introduction
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC [Databricks TPC-DI](https://github.com/shannon-barrow/databricks-tpc-di) is an implementation of specifications derived from the [TPC-DI](http://tpc.org/tpcdi/default5.asp) Benchmark. In addition to facilitating a data architecture suitable for standardized benchmarking, this code demonstrates the mechanics of a typical Data Integration ETL application. The code uses software provided by the TPC project to do this. [Follow this link](https://www.tpc.org/TPC_Documents_Current_Versions/download_programs/tools-download-request5.asp?bm_type=TPC-DI&bm_vers=1.1.0&mode=CURRENT-ONLY) for further information or if you want to access the TPC software yourself.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ### Default options
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Those familiar with [Databricks TPC-DI](https://github.com/shannon-barrow/databricks-tpc-di) will know that the process is quite configurable. This notebook provides a derivation of this work that is tuned to the specific needs of this training environment. This allows us to use a dataset following TPC-DI specifications to demonstrate an assortment of data warehousing tasks using the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Specifically, the significant parameter settings are as follows:
-- MAGIC - **Scale Factor**: this correlates to how much data will be processed. Neither the total number of files and tables processed nor the workflow DAG are affected, although the amount of data per file will be. In this configuration, a scale factor of 10 is used, which aligns to roughly 1GB of raw data.
-- MAGIC - **Workflow Type**: controls the underlying type of compute. In this configuration, we leverage a pre-configured SQL warehouse to do an incremental (benchmarked) run, or execute all batches in one pass.

-- COMMAND ----------

