-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Data generation
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Data generation involves creating raw data in various formats, as required by the TPC specification. The raw data is generated by a software component provided by TPC. The steps in the data generation are as follows:
-- MAGIC * Copy the TPC-provided artifact (`DIGen.jar`) and its dependencies to the driver node execution environment (these are stored in the *./tools/datagen* subfolder).
-- MAGIC * Execute a python wrapper script that invokes the data generator, which will generate data files in the driver node's local file system (in the */localdisk0/tmp/tpcdi* folder).
-- MAGIC * Copy the generated files into a volume. The target volume is in the output of the previous cell.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC For brevity, the raw data is pre-generated in this lab environment, so the tool will skip this step since it notices that the data has already been generated.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %run ./Includes/tools/data_generator

-- COMMAND ----------

